Subject: genhd: fixup kobj_to_dev() macro
From: Pavel Emelyanov <xemul@openvz.org>

Using "kobj" twice is not OK, because substitution will be done twice
resulting in compile breakage if variable name is different from structure
member name.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Emelyanov <xemul@openvz.org>
Signed-off-by: Alexey Dobriyan <adobriyan@sw.ru>
Cc: Greg KH <greg@kroah.com>
Cc: Kay Sievers <kay.sievers@vrfy.org>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---

 include/linux/genhd.h |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff -puN include/linux/genhd.h~gregkh-driver-block-device-genhd-fixup-kobj_to_dev-macro include/linux/genhd.h
--- a/include/linux/genhd.h~gregkh-driver-block-device-genhd-fixup-kobj_to_dev-macro
+++ a/include/linux/genhd.h
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_BLOCK
 
-#define kobj_to_dev(kobj) container_of(kobj, struct device, kobj)
+#define kobj_to_dev(k) container_of(k, struct device, kobj)
 #define dev_to_disk(device) container_of(device, struct gendisk, dev)
 #define dev_to_part(device) container_of(device, struct hd_struct, dev)
 
